        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Montague Island, Narooma, New South Wales\n- Topics: geography, place names\n\nFacts:\n- Montague Island is an 81 ha reserve and island located about 9 km southeast of Narooma.\n- Narooma is the nearest onshore town to Montague Island.\n- Narooma is located on the Princes Highway in New South Wales.\n- The name Narooma is said to come from an Aboriginal word meaning “clear blue waters.”",
